          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+physics"} particle physics
            the letters
            %em MSSM
            are an abbreviation for “minimally supersymmetric standard model”: an extension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+particle+phyiscs%29"} model (in particle phyiscs)
            with a minimum amount of extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+symmetry"} global
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+QCD"} super QCD
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R-parity"} R-parity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+model"} intersecting D-brane model
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+coupling+unification"} gauge coupling unification
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} supersymmetry and Calabi-Yau manifolds
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original articles:
          %ul
            %li
              %p S. Dimopoulos and H. Georgi, Phys. Lett. B 117, 287 (1982).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                , Phys. Rev. D 26, 287 (1982)
          %p Theoretical predictions:
          %ul
            %li
              Stefano Frixione, Benjamin Fuks, Valentin Hirschi, Kentarou Mawatari, Hua-Sheng Shao, Marthijn P. A. Sunder, Marco Zaro,
              %em Automated simulations beyond the Standard Model: supersymmetry
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.04898"}> arXiv:1907.04898
              )
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sven+Krippendorf"}> Sven Krippendorf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Quevedo"} Fernando Quevedo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oliver+Schlotterer"} Oliver Schlotterer
                %em Cambridge Lectures on Supersymmetry and Extra Dimensions
                (2010) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.1491"}> arXiv:1011.1491
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/875723"} spire:875723
            %li
              %p
                S. F. King, S. Moretti, R. Nevzorov,
                %em A Review of the Exceptional Supersymmetric Standard Model
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.02788"}> arXiv:2002.02788
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Dine"}> Michael Dine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and string theory: beyond the standard model
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/ae/academic/subjects/physics/particle-physics-and-nuclear-physics/supersymmetry-and-string-theory-beyond-standard-model-2nd-edition?format=HB"} ISBN:9781009290920
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.nucleares.unam.mx/~alberto/apuntes/dine.pdf"} pdf
          %p On the experimental status:
          %ul
            %li
              Hyun Min Lee:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetry and LHC era
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Particle+Physics"} Encyclopedia of Particle Physics
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.01769"}> arXiv:2505.01769
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#relation_to_flavour_anomalies Relation to flavour anomalies
          %p
            Suggestion that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R-parity"} R-parity
            violation could explain the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
          %ul
            %li#WangYangYuan19
              %p
                Dong-Yang Wang, Ya-Dong Yang, Xing-Bo Yuan,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi c
                        %mi τ
                        %mover
                          %mi ν
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \to c \tau \bar \nu
                  decays in supersymmetry with R-parity violation
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.08784"}> arXiv:1905.08784
                )
            %li
              %p
                Quan-Yi Hu, Lin-Lin Huang,
                %em
                  Explaining
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo →
                        %mi s
                        %msup
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\to s \ell^+ \ell^-
                  data by sneutrinos in the R-parity violating MSSM
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.03676"}> arXiv:1912.03676
                )
            %li
              %p
                Quan-Yi Hu, Ya-Dong Yang, Min-Di Zheng,
                %em Revisiting the B-physics anomalies in R-parity violating MSSM
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.09875"}> arXiv:2002.09875
                )
            %li
              %p
                Wolfgang Altmannshofer, P. S. Bhupal Dev, Amarjit Soni, Yicong Sui,
                %em
                  Addressing
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi D
                                %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{D^\ast}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi K
                                %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_{K^\ast}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g-2
                  and ANITA anomalies in a minimal R-parity violating supersymmetric framework
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.12910"}> arXiv:2002.12910
                )
          %h3#ReferencesInHeteroticStringTheory In heterotic string theory
          %p
            The origin of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down approach
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            due to (
            %a{:href => "heterotic+string#CHSW85"}> Candelas-Horowitz-Strominger-Witten 85
            ).
          %p
            A brief review of motivations for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            models in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Witten02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quest For Unification
              %a{:href => "http://www.desy.de/susy02/"} SUSY 2002
              at DESY, Hamburg (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0207124"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0207124
              )
          %p
            The following articles establish the existences of exact realization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            and
            = succeed "-content" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            (not yet checking
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+couplings"} Yukawa couplings
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Braun"}> Volker Braun
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"} Tony Pantev
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Heterotic Standard Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501070"} arXiv:hep-th/0501070
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Braun"}> Volker Braun
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Pantev"} Tony Pantev
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Exact MSSM Spectrum from String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512177"} arXiv:hep-th/0512177
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Bouchard"}> Vincent Bouchard
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"} Ron Donagi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An SU(5) Heterotic Standard Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512149"} arXiv:hep-th/0512149
          %p
            A computer search through the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"}> landscape
            ” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+varieties"} Calabi-Yau varieties
            showed several hundreds more such exact heterotic standard models (about one billionth of all CYs searched, and most of them arising as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUTs"} GUTs
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Heterotic Compactification, An Algorithmic Approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0702210"} arXiv:hep-th/0702210
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                , James Gray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"} Eran Palti
                %em Two Hundred Heterotic Standard Models on Smooth Calabi-Yau Threefolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4804"}> arXiv:1106.4804
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                , James Gray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"} Eran Palti
                %em Heterotic Line Bundle Standard Models
                JHEP06(2012)113 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1202.1757"}> arXiv:1202.1757
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                , Andrei Constantin, James Gray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"} Eran Palti
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Comprehensive Scan for Heterotic SU(5) GUT models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1307.4787"} arXiv:1307.4787
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"}> Yang-Hui He
                , Seung-Joo Lee,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                %em Heterotic Model Building: 16 Special Manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1309.0223"}> arXiv:1309.0223
                )
            %li#CHE18
              %p
                Andrei Constantin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                %em Counting String Theory Standard Models
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.00444"}> arXiv:1810.00444
                )
          %p The resulting database of compactifications is here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
              , James Gray,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"} Eran Palti
              %em Heterotic standard model database
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/projects/CalabiYau/linebundlemodels/index.html."}> web
              )
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em New aspects of heterotic geometry and phenomenology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwth.mpp.mpg.de/conf/strings2012/"} Strings2012
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwth.mpp.mpg.de/members/strings/strings2012/strings_files/program/Talks/Wednesday/Anderson.pdf"} pdf
            %li#He18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"}> Yang-Hui He
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deep-learning the landscape
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://ims.nus.edu.sg/events/2018/wstring/wk.php"} String and M-Theory: The new geometry of the 21st century
                (
                %a{:href => "https://ims.nus.edu.sg/events/2018/wstring/files/yang.pdf"}> pdf slides
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x3ThgBgkPlE"} video recording
          %p
            Computation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metrics"} metrics
            on these Calabi-Yau compactifications (eventually needed for computing their induced
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+couplings"} Yukawa couplings
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Braun"}> Volker Braun
              , Tamaz Brelidze,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"} Michael Douglas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
              = succeed "," do
                %em Calabi-Yau Metrics for Quotients and Complete Intersections
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0712.3563"} arXiv:0712.3563
          %p This “heterotic standard model” has a “hidden sector” copy of the actual standard model, more details of which are discussed here:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Braun"}> Volker Braun
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
              %em Supersymmetric Hidden Sectors for Heterotic Standard Models
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.6767"}> arXiv:1301.6767
              )
          %p
            The issue of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
            in these kinds of models is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Michele Cicoli, Senarath de Alwis, Alexander Westphal,
                %em Heterotic Moduli Stabilization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.1809"}> arXiv:1304.1809
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lara+Anderson"}> Lara Anderson
                , James Gray,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
                %em Vacuum Varieties, Holomorphic Bundles and Complex Structure Stabilization in Heterotic Theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.2704"}> arXiv:1304.2704
                )
          %p Principles singling out heterotic models with three generations of fundamental particles are discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Candelas"}> Philip Candelas
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xenia+de+la+Ossa"} Xenia de la Ossa
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Hui+He"} Yang-Hui He
              = succeed "," do
                %em Triadophilia: A Special Corner in the Landscape
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.3134"} arXiv:0706.3134
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Hajime Otsuka,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 32
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(32)
                  heterotic line bundle models
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.03684"} arXiv:1801.03684
          %h3#in_ftheory In F-theory
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering"} geometric engineering
            of the MSSM in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
          %ul
            %li#CLLO18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cveti%C4%8D"}> Mirjam Cvetič
              , Ling Lin, Muyang Liu, Paul-Konstantin Oehlmann,
              %em
                An F-theory Realization of the Chiral MSSM with
                = succeed "-Parity" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.01320"}> arXiv:1807.01320
              )
          %p
            A large number of realizations of the exact field content of the MSSM in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            is claimed to be realized in
          %ul
            %li#CveticHalversonLinLiuTian19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Halverson"} James Halverson
              %em A Quadrillion Standard Models from F-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.00009"}> arXiv:1903.00009
              )
          %h3#experimental_status  Experimental status
          %ul
            %li
              Jin Min Yang, Pengxuan Zhu, Rui Zhu,
              %em A brief survey of low energy supersymmetry under current experiments
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.06686"}> arXiv:2211.06686
              )
